# ─── Monorepo: XRUFY ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Install: npm install
# Dev (web + server): npm run dev
#   Root `predev` frees port 4000 so the API child process can bind (avoids stale Node/tsx).
#   If 3000 is busy, Next picks another port (e.g. 3001) — use the URL printed in the terminal.
#
# Web:   http://localhost:3000 (or the port Next prints)
# API:   http://127.0.0.1:4000/health
#
# Forms on the site POST to /api/forms on the web origin; Next.js proxies
# to the server (see web/next.config.ts). Override with SERVER_ORIGIN if needed.

# web/.env.local (optional)
# SERVER_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:4000

# server/.env (copy from server/.env.example)
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://xrufy:xrufy@127.0.0.1:5432/xrufy
# WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
# Then create tables: npm run db:push -w @xrufy/server
#
# Server deploy (Docker): see deploy/README.md and deploy/docker-compose.yml
